        <font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> <BLOCKQUOTE id=quote><font size=1 face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" id=quote>quote:<hr height=1 noshade id=quote><BR>Mass PvP is where it's going to be at soon.  </P><P>If you want *IMHO* the most dominating battlefield PvP class/builds go Shadow Priest or Ice Mage.    The ONLY reason I beat them 40% of the time is that I bluff them out. 10% of the time I simply outsmart them, the rest of the time I'm laying a freezing trap and hauling ass the other way.</P><P>Mages with manashield, blink hard hitting nukes are just damn near unstoppable.  To me they are the premier PvP class.<BR><hr height=1 noshade id=quote></BLOCKQUOTE id=quote></font id=quote><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size=2 id=quote></P><P>I'm not sure if I'll like PvP, but since the PvP 101 thread made it sound so fun, I plan on giving it a try.  I'll keep in mind that the Frost Mage might be better...  I had assumed that the typical 31 Arcane/20 Fire would be the way to go.</P><P>Now that I check this great mage talent faq, I see that they suggest Frost will shine in battlegrounds:</P><P><a href="http://forums.worldofwarcraft.com/thread.aspx?fn=wow-mage&t=23&p=1&tmp=1#post23" target="_blank">http://forums.worldofwarcraft.com/thread.aspx?fn=wow-mage&t=23&p=1&tmp=1#post23</a></P><P>If anyone is thinking of leveling a mage for PvP, check out that faq for the level progression for buying talents.  Fire and Arcane are the way to go for PvE, at least through 40 and probably through 50.</P><P>Of course, if mages are as good as you say in PvP, I expect the nerf bat to follow soon after battlegrounds.  <img src=icon_smile_tongue.gif border=0 align=middle></P><P><BR>Inferna 49 Mage<BR><a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
