        <font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Well I don't know much about rogues but the best build for a pvp warrior would be 31/20 arms/fury, but not dual wield. The best thing you can do is use an arcanite reaper and take the axe spec, that will give you an extra 5% chance to crit and since the dmg is dealt with 1 swing its easier, nobody is just gonna stand around and let a dual wield warrior swing away. I have seen vidoes of warriors hitting for 600+ a hit with that, since its not hard to get your crit chance over 30% if your a very high end warrior. My crit chance is 20% now and I am only in my mid 40's.</P><P>Jobee Night Elf Warrior<BR><a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
