        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?ARCHIVE=&method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=50651&TOPIC_ID=8308&FORUM_ID=27&CAT_ID=6&Forum_Title=World+of+Warcraft&Topic_Title=Which+of+these+is+better+and+why%3F&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> <BLOCKQUOTE id=quote><font size=1 face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" id=quote>quote:<hr height=1 noshade id=quote>Well I don't know much about rogues but the best build for a pvp warrior would be 31/20 arms/fury, but not dual wield. The best thing you can do is use an arcanite reaper and take the axe spec, that will give you an extra 5% chance to crit and since the dmg is dealt with 1 swing its easier, nobody is just gonna stand around and let a dual wield warrior swing away. I have seen vidoes of warriors hitting for 600+ a hit with that, since its not hard to get your crit chance over 30% if your a very high end warrior. My crit chance is 20% now and I am only in my mid 40's. <hr height=1 noshade id=quote></BLOCKQUOTE id=quote></font id=quote><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size=2 id=quote></P><P>Here's the thing Jobee, you won't get to do that in PvP battles.  Duels? Sure.  Sometimes in the field? Maybe.</P><P>1) If I see the warrior out there I drop a freeze trap and wait.  Warriors know they can beat hunters once in melee range so....CHARGE!!!! BAM.  They're stuck on my frost trap.  I'll let you sit there a few while I prance off and lay another trap.  Your rage goes down (espically annoying if they took a rage potion).  Then I aimshot, concussion shot, viper sting, sic pet.  About the time you get close to me concussion shot is wore off, oops hit my freeze trap.  I'm still spinning around out of melee range plunking you with arrows.  This is repeted until warrior is dead.  It's not 100% effective, but easily 90% of the time I kill the warrior.   BTW Crit builds don't have high defense, so even post-patch they're going to be walking pincoushins for hunters.</P><P>2) As Kanr, I see the warrior start to charge, I slam bear form.  Now it's like you're fighting another warrior except I can stun you, root you heal myself nuke you, go back bear and do it again.   I beat paladins AND warriors like this routinely.  Crit warriors have crap for defense so it's easy.</P><P>3) Protection spec warriors eat you for lunch on the field.</P><P>4) Frost mages snare and kite you while blasting for full damage.</P><P>5) Shadow priests fear you, lay on a billion dots, fear you while draining life.  When you finally get through with all that you're nearly dead, they're full health and you gotta chew thrrough their bubble.</P><P>6) Because you don't have the defensive capabilities and +defense of a protection spec war, rogues eat you alive.   Without high ABS and Dodge they stunlock you and beat you down on the field.</P><P>7) Shaman throw grounding totems and kite you till you die of old age.</P><P>8) Paladins beat you down, if you do more damage to them than they to you, they heal up and continue beating you down.  If they get in trouble they bubble up and heal while the best you can do is bandage with first aid.</P><P>9) Warocks mez you with their pet while laying dots, then fearkite you till you're nearly dead.  By the time you actually can get TO them to do damage you're still going to have to cut through their healthstone as well as the billion hitpoints most of them have.</P><P>10) All of these strats are made worse by the fact if everybody else sees a warrior with a big arse axe or sword on the field, we KNOW your spec and gang up on you apropriately.  The only use I've seen for crit warriors is to charge into the "british army lines" that invariably form and use fear just before you die to help try and break the line.</P><P>In duels? Ya crit warriors are useful.   In PvE 58+? Useless, can't tank, can't hold agro.  In Large scale PvP? Useless, no way to defend yourself against ganks , no way to hide, no way to heal other than 2 minute potion timer and first aid.  DPS output negelagable compared to rogue in melee combat, well below casters.</P><P><BR>Not meaning to burst your bubble or anything, just warning you of how things *really* will be for you out there.<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
