        &nbsp;<a href="post.asp?ARCHIVE=&method=ReplyQuote&REPLY_ID=50652&TOPIC_ID=8308&FORUM_ID=27&CAT_ID=6&Forum_Title=World+of+Warcraft&Topic_Title=Which+of+these+is+better+and+why%3F&M="><img src="icon_reply_topic.gif" height=15 width=15 alt="Reply with Quote" border="0" align="absmiddle" hspace="6"></a>

        <hr noshade size="1">
        
        <font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> Based on my limited pvp experience, your mileage may vary, no warranties express or implied:</P><P>Syl, if you are going to rely on sinister strike (which a heavy combat build indicates), you are going to be better off with swords or maces, so you want sword or mace spec instead of dagger spec.  If you want to use daggers, you need to focus on the various backstab/ambush talents.</P><P>You'll want improved sinister strike, as that cost reduction lets you get off those SS's that much more quickly.  You could probably cut 2 points from dual wield spec for that.  Pvp fights aren't going to last long enough for your off hand damage to make that much of a diference.</P><P>I probably wouldn't go with Remorseless attacks.  In mass pvp, as soon as you destealth you are going to become a primary target, so you want to kill a soft target and get the hell out of there, if you can.  Improved eviscerate and murder might be a better choice.  You can play around with it to see if it helps, but I think you want to focus on abilities that let you take your current target down faster, not stuff to help you if you take on a second target within 20 seconds.</P><P>For weapon choice, sword or mace is mostly a personal choice.  I have 5 points in mace spec currently.  It goes off frequently enough that stun immunity kicks in on longer fights.  On average I'd say it goes off about once every fight at least.  The 5% chance seems low, but using two maces makes it go off quite a bit.  Presumably sword spec would go off as frequently.</P><P>Whether you go mace or sword, you want a slow, high damage range weapon in your main hand and a fast fast weapon in your off hand.  If you want to be able to ambush/backstab, get a weaponswap mod.  Without heavy ambush/backstab spec, though, I think you would be better off sticking with cheap shot and SS (unless you come across a wounded target, where a good ambush might take them out).  If you go for a dagger build, you also want a slow, high damage range dagger main hand and fast weapon off-hand.</P><P>From watching the AH, there appears to be greater choice in high damage swords than maces, but you can get a good pair of high end swords or maces far more easily than you can get a good pair of high end daggers (by easily, meaning buying at AH versus trying to get BoP instance drops).</P><P>For pvp, an ambush/backstab build might be better, overall, since they tend to aim for cold blood and preparation, which gives you an automatic reset of your timer abilities and a crit on command, which makes for very painful ambushes.  That build is better for stunlock, as well, since the preparation ability will give you another vanish/cheapshot/kidney shot round of stunlock.</P><P>Cristos 20 Human Palading Smith/Mine<BR>Umbra Human Warlock Tailor/?<BR>Rhualg Elf Hunter Leather/Skinning</P><P>Who do you want to twink today?<a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
      </tr>

