        <font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"> I have a dorf rogue too, just haven't put too much time into either of them.  I originally envisioned a duel wielding axe warrior or dagger rogue with high crit and dodge, but it sounds like at least for the warrior thats not viable in pvp. I am wary of rolling a rogue just because there are so many of them already.</P><P>So I am gonna be building up Lilnuka (what ever happened to the GI anyway? ) and Yew, my druid. Wolflad seems to move around the battlefield in southshore so effortlessly which I admire. The versatility of being able to stealth, absorb melee damage, nuke and heal all in one class seems like a nice package. I don't see any battlegrounds planned for underground, so the loss of some abilities there won't be a big loss.</P><P>I sure wish Warriors were viable in pvp though, they should be. Does their trinket break root? Do the ornate leggs and belt break out off the freezing traps too? Is there a timer on your putting down traps?</P><P><a href="#top"><img src="icon_go_up.gif" height=15 width=15 border="0" align="right" alt="Go to Top of Page"></a></font></td>
